[2.25, "o", "cluster: demo\r\ncontrol plane: proofdemo2036341\r\nhost group: remote-linux\r\napi endpoint: https://demo-k3s.internal:6443\r\nstable-endpoint posture: manual-rewrite-required\r\nstable-endpoint detail: Hosted AWS x86_64 PVM stable endpoint posture is manual-rewrite-required: Port hands off configured api_endpoint 'https://demo-k3s.internal:6443' but this topology still declares 1 control-plane microVM with scheduler 'spread'. Losing the selected control-plane guest would still require manual downstream rewrites or unsupported operator intervention.\r\ncontrol-plane machines: cloud-generic\r\nworker machines: cloud-aws\r\ncontrol-plane launch: cloud-generic pid=2036364 runtime-dir=/tmp/phk3s-t5hzfo8p/rt/g/cloud-generic\r\nworker launch: cloud-aws pid=2037648 runtime-dir=/tmp/phk3s-t5hzfo8p/rt/a/cloud-aws\r\nboundary: Hosted K3s requires one hosted control plane and one host group with live placement capacity in this slice.\r\nboundary: Hosted K3s remains stateless in this slice; attached volumes, persistent storage, and CSI are out of scope.\r\nboundary: Real HA requires at least three control-plane microVMs, a stable HTTPS api endpoint that fronts them, and placement across distinct execution hosts; Port models the endpoint but does not ship the load balancer, VIP, or ingress layer itself in this slice.\r\nboundary: This config declares 1 control-plane microVM with scheduler 'spread'; Port classifies that topology as non-HA until at least 3 control-plane microVMs and spread scheduling are both present.\r\nboundary: Control-plane scheduler 'spread' requires newly placed control-plane microVMs to land on distinct eligible execution hosts and fails placement instead of collapsing onto an already used host.\r\n"]
